vironment variable. I should also look for references related to the payload involved in this process. It might be helpful to inspect existing skill patterns, particularly focusing on nephrology patterns, to see what I can adapt or learn from. It's all about ensuring I'm organizing everything correctly while making sure I cover all necessary angles!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xBOhLmXGDxL0iHwBSSDzN8bl|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8a30d7c8191932243e8a70b85c3","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/SKILL.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_CfLYwtensDHeej854awDlNn4|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8a30d888191884406bc10e0403f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"find /home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":947,"output":142,"cacheRead":14464,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15553,"cost":{"input":0.0023675000000000002,"output":0.00213,"cacheRead":0.003616,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0081135}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774446750675}}
{"type":"message","id":"e0f5576e","parentId":"9f3bdff0","timestamp":"2026-03-25T13:52:35.216Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_xBOhLmXGDxL0iHwBSSDzN8bl|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8a30d7c8191932243e8a70b85c3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: nephrology-klm\ndescription: Query the Nephrology-KLM knowledge model for nephrology expertise, differential-diagnosis support, disease-specific interpretation, and specialized kidney-related feedback. Use when the user needs nephrology-domain guidance about CKD, AKI, glomerular disease, dialysis, electrolyte/acid-base disorders, renal imaging findings, nephrology treatment considerations, or kidney-focused diagnosis/expertise.\n---\n\n# Nephrology KLM\n\nQuery the remote Nephrology-KLM endpoint and translate its output into safe, concise nephrology-oriented guidance.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the request is nephrology-specific.\n   - Use this skill for kidney disease, renal oncology, nephrology treatment questions, renal function interpretation, dialysis topics, electrolyte or acid-base issues, and nephrology differential support.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\n\n2. Build the prompt.\n   - Use the user's question directly when it is already specific.\n   - If the user provides case details, summarize them into one clear nephrology prompt.\n   - If assumptions are needed, state them explicitly.\n\n3. Call the endpoint.\n   - Run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py \"<prompt>\"\n```\n\n- The script sends:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"name\": \"nephrology-klm\",\n    \"workflow_name\": \"nephrology-klm\",\n    \"workflow_type\": \"experiment\",\n    \"workflow_id\": \"nephrology-klm\",\n    \"workflow_run_id\": \"manual\",\n    \"run_id\": \"manual\"\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"prompt\": \"<prompt>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- Endpoint:\n  `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8001/nodes/ai_tool/Nephrology-KLM-model`\n\n4. Read the response.\n   - Prefer the returned `data.Answer` field.\n   - If that field contains a JSON string, extract the `answer` text when possible.\n   - If parsing fails, return the raw answer text and note the ambiguity.\n\n5. Respond safely.\n   - Summarize the nephrology answer in plain language.\n   - Separate model output from your own cautionary framing.\n   - Avoid presenting the KLM output as certain or as a substitute for clinician judgment.\n   - If urgent red flags appear, recommend prompt in-person medical evaluation.\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn:\n\n- **Nephrology KLM answer**: short excerpt or the full answer if compact\n- **Plain-language summary**: the main nephrology takeaway\n- **Important cautions / next steps**: especially when diagnosis or treatment decisions need clinical confirmation\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774446755209}}
{"type":"message","id":"37228fe9","parentId":"e0f5576e","timestamp":"2026-03-25T13:52:35.223Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CfLYwtensDHeej854awDlNn4|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8a30d888191884406bc10e0403f","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/SKILL.md\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":9,"aggregated":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/SKILL.md\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774446755219}}
{"type":"message","id":"c58564c4","parentId":"37228fe9","timestamp":"2026-03-25T13:52:37.236Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3CpL1MWlCQCsPhDUUCx6McB5|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8a4a0248191984097359a5583be","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":798,"output":40,"cacheRead":15360,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16198,"cost":{"input":0.0019950000000000002,"output":0.0006000000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0038399999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.006435}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774446755222}}
{"type":"message","id":"8a615b49","parentId":"c58564c4","timestamp":"2026-03-25T13:52:37.250Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3CpL1MWlCQCsPhDUUCx6McB5|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8a4a0248191984097359a5583be","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\nENDPOINT = \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8001/nodes/ai_tool/Nephrology-KLM-model\"\n\n\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return body.strip()\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n    data = parsed.get(\"data\")\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        answer = data.get(\"Answer\") or data.get(\"answer\") or data.get(\"ANSWER\")\n        if answer is not None:\n            if isinstance(answer, str):\n                text = answer.strip()\n                try:\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict) and \"answer\" in nested:\n                        return str(nested[\"answer\"])\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    pass\n                return text\n            return json.dumps(answer, indent=2)\n\n    for key in (\"Answer\", \"answer\", \"ANSWER\"):\n        if key in parsed:\n            value = parsed[key]\n            return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n\ndef call_endpoint(prompt: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\n    payload = json.dumps({\n        \"metadata\": {\n            \"name\": \"nephrology-klm\",\n            \"workflow_name\": \"nephrology-klm\",\n            \"workflow_type\": \"experiment\",\n            \"workflow_id\": \"nephrology-klm\",\n            \"workflow_run_id\": \"manual\",\n            \"run_id\": \"manual\",\n        },\n        \"data\": {\"prompt\": prompt},\n    }).encode(\"utf-8\")\n    req = request.Request(\n        ENDPOINT,\n        data=payload,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            body = resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Request failed: {e}\") from e\n\n    return extract_answer(body)\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Query the Nephrology-KLM endpoint and print the returned answer\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"prompt\", help=\"Nephrology prompt to send to the model\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=45)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.prompt, timeout=args.timeout)\n    print(answer)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774446757244}}
{"type":"message","id":"fd23ed6a","parentId":"8a615b49","timestamp":"2026-03-25T13:53:16.263Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Creating a blank endpoint**\n\nI need to establish a similar but blank endpoint, which might include a config reference. The user wants the endpoint left blank for now, so I'll set it to ENDPOINT=\"\" and make sure to clear any error if it's unset. \n\nThe skill should guide how to gather necessary info from the conversation. I might include references to prompt templates in the documentation. Let’s move forward with creating a concise skill and script, and include relevant files like references/prompting.md or api-contract.md.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8a738f08191b0e686ad84045ef4\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpw-iq034C89pt1JSsOrQhxFRplWph4737lBr298q73P4gVvw5sRXSOih2962KC_UF_1RRxk4aoJfKElA6vQkEohmXfXSKNGlaVHW_vwzQeYhiEGBdp9RUTkelH6qTp3Kjrcg_rmdHTylKEBaHyCp12Cv1PD83-RduL3Q986YmGnpn6OT9XP0ybdn_Rup5B53Fl4378uLSrxt9QAKlsJMY8ajheJZFwKksDrjfvFkWXGLmwObf22Qljz6JePT2PiCMyhiHkWe857jeWqMqRd4FkDSs27E9FATNi3OggnvKag52ClWkAP7ciM9U-wbHbwZouEnMTGsDQEriIFEeL3Z1I9r_F8t3I8lApeZlpgirw78Olr5rk8LKwFljE7MmVrrOBK7_EFxfWDWA47vwa2Yt7LGLGX31IaFEZsyclEnIlwlda6iSTbUMLnZq3Ah_b2YS9QtwX8P6fop9Q95G06eXaIw8zTcoyT6fH0D1b85Pner9_FnunETVjtMcnEaG120nX8JlamoR2Qc8zR4yIVDGJ8sxUkQApFHOE5LLeLSbovzyj_c2VFeYlhTtceeckg-KCc-6amwj-tnvTvKmC0eOIcX23HpENfhCbwuljeTfh3WRmwodh4ZwyNgp1xHF4KLExhxiKESwEQtMFROY2HRwF80AqqBgXRPZshN76MDqTZlYftO0laMMrjzpZKeknSWSKwwl1lM530zzPqCaGjoj-v30T_uMkWuzJY3QTXCTmQowQd3AFRH6cCjofPaWlWPQt33LjbFF121TggtjMzS8KHyT1C65l5Q-W6l93Bt72gFO6cbeAdUwPxXG_U8hqFw0AtdPgCD4ivBeHlIOYZpla9nai5_b5ui6ghLPEp_ALPiW4zwE30WGvC07yCxIzaZ33kTczAWTX13oyEgJf1FcbnUlNhr5_Yx8MK-3My-CEUIiRHZIA8NZEUx7glMzi3fs_KZn9cDcaAvXWyvf3rdvaYEXdioK_xhITQOy6sf3blCIxiX9iX-88a0ROEks-rtYpzlPgTllY6PUIn6HBW4J9PyOhBxfW2NNhDSxA15YWkOwxoGEUfBJ5Ns7lQB3Dx-WcKNbYcCxSM0-JLuw5aLpa7IluTMzcioZ0lEDyuJM5FMbY9GRD7UtETG6ruRdknPoZHS6tUccztOaEc4gS6hd0N6TJOtg2_WwURLnKUrlWuliKVRpWWvhiorxLp5TanS-WGWgExwbQ01z4VCyViY7VsyWT8gVPY-OVzeZa0GVKpZg4a8tvmgUNkFkkDj2O-7qawp1fUuiPhZqL3ePl5xxThU5iLdT3Hy_1ZH9R22IyNZRJGcPfkF7mpWlNa_53pWREOgjokaY5RiuIdV0klkH49EwKfXwNBJ6pg6jS1vpvK3s-7-yHxSHJ5EmYT0Fcm6gtktz0YUTJMgO1M7sVktKZxJ7-_eqnMN-J6_fIGBN7OeLWyfw2Ybmrfup4KV_BqFpRV5oXe1sMgbv8kyvr5qmQKdVwvjL8AbgM3Tv4WjXJ4BnfBw=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Creating a blank endpoint**\\n\\nI need to establish a similar but blank endpoint, which might include a config reference. The user wants the endpoint left blank for now, so I'll set it to ENDPOINT=\\\"\\\" and make sure to clear any error if it's unset. \\n\\nThe skill should guide how to gather necessary info from the conversation. I might include references to prompt templates in the documentation. Let’s move forward with creating a concise skill and script, and include relevant files like references/prompting.md or api-contract.md.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I found a close existing pattern and I’m basing this new skill on it, but making it conversation-aware and leaving the endpoint intentionally unconfigured.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8aad9a48191ad6a85d7b3ba3973\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ZetP2sgYVPGUQR7PPCjjuCA3|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8cc006c8191b179b7137693c024","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: slm-nephrology\ndescription: Contact a nephrology-focused small language model (SLM) endpoint, sending a compact but complete nephrology case summary derived from the current conversation and the user’s request, then return the model’s answer in a safe and readable way. Use when the user wants nephrology-specialist feedback, kidney-focused interpretation, renal differential support, electrolyte/acid-base nephrology input, CKD/AKI guidance, dialysis-related reasoning, renal imaging interpretation, or any request that should be routed to a nephrology-expert SLM.\n---\n\n# SLM Nephrology\n\nRoute nephrology-specific requests to the dedicated SLM endpoint after building a focused summary from the conversation.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the request is nephrology-specific.\n   - Use this skill for kidney disease, renal function interpretation, CKD, AKI, glomerular disease, electrolyte or acid-base issues, dialysis, renal imaging findings, nephrology treatment considerations, kidney-focused differential diagnosis, and related specialist interpretation.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\n\n2. Build a compact nephrology brief from the conversation.\n   - Include the user’s exact question or ask.\n   - Include the clinically or technically relevant context already present in the conversation.\n   - Prefer concise structured bullets over a long paragraph.\n   - When available, include:\n     - demographics if relevant\n     - key symptoms and timeline\n     - important PMH / renal history\n     - medications relevant to nephrology\n     - labs, vitals, urinalysis, imaging, pathology, or prior assessments\n     - red flags, uncertainty, or missing data\n   - Do not invent facts. If something important is missing, say it is unknown.\n\n3. Call the endpoint.\n   - Run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py \"<brief>\"\n```\n\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"name\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n    \"workflow_name\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n    \"workflow_type\": \"experiment\",\n    \"workflow_id\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n    \"workflow_run_id\": \"manual\",\n    \"run_id\": \"manual\"\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"prompt\": \"<brief>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n   - The endpoint is intentionally left blank in `scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py` and must be filled in before the skill can be used.\n\n4. Read the response.\n   - Prefer `data.Answer`.\n   - Accept `data.answer`, `Answer`, or `answer` if the endpoint returns a different casing.\n   - If the returned answer is itself JSON encoded as a string, extract the nested `answer` field when possible.\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, return the best raw text available and say so briefly.\n\n5. Return the answer safely.\n   - Present the nephrology SLM’s answer clearly.\n   - If useful, add a short plain-language summary.\n   - Keep uncertainty visible.\n   - Do not present the SLM output as a confirmed diagnosis.\n   - If urgent renal or systemic red flags appear, recommend prompt clinician evaluation.\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn:\n\n- **Nephrology SLM answer**: the specialist-model answer, lightly cleaned up if needed\n- **Key takeaway**: short summary in plain language when helpful\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when clinically relevant or when important data is missing\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: slm-nephrology\\ndescription: Contact a nephrology-focused small language model (SLM) endpoint, sending a compact but complete nephrology case summary derived from the current conversation and the user’s request, then return the model’s answer in a safe and readable way. Use when the user wants nephrology-specialist feedback, kidney-focused interpretation, renal differential support, electrolyte/acid-base nephrology input, CKD/AKI guidance, dialysis-related reasoning, renal imaging interpretation, or any request that should be routed to a nephrology-expert SLM.\\n---\\n\\n# SLM Nephrology\\n\\nRoute nephrology-specific requests to the dedicated SLM endpoint after building a focused summary from the conversation.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Confirm the request is nephrology-specific.\\n   - Use this skill for kidney disease, renal function interpretation, CKD, AKI, glomerular disease, electrolyte or acid-base issues, dialysis, renal imaging findings, nephrology treatment considerations, kidney-focused differential diagnosis, and related specialist interpretation.\\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\\n\\n2. Build a compact nephrology brief from the conversation.\\n   - Include the user’s exact question or ask.\\n   - Include the clinically or technically relevant context already present in the conversation.\\n   - Prefer concise structured bullets over a long paragraph.\\n   - When available, include:\\n     - demographics if relevant\\n     - key symptoms and timeline\\n     - important PMH / renal history\\n     - medications relevant to nephrology\\n     - labs, vitals, urinalysis, imaging, pathology, or prior assessments\\n     - red flags, uncertainty, or missing data\\n   - Do not invent facts. If something important is missing, say it is unknown.\\n\\n3. Call the endpoint.\\n   - Run:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py \\\"<brief>\\\"\\n```\\n\\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"slm-nephrology\\\",\\n    \\\"workflow_name\\\": \\\"slm-nephrology\\\",\\n    \\\"workflow_type\\\": \\\"experiment\\\",\\n    \\\"workflow_id\\\": \\\"slm-nephrology\\\",\\n    \\\"workflow_run_id\\\": \\\"manual\\\",\\n    \\\"run_id\\\": \\\"manual\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"data\\\": {\\n    \\\"prompt\\\": \\\"<brief>\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n   - The endpoint is intentionally left blank in `scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py` and must be filled in before the skill can be used.\\n\\n4. Read the response.\\n   - Prefer `data.Answer`.\\n   - Accept `data.answer`, `Answer`, or `answer` if the endpoint returns a different casing.\\n   - If the returned answer is itself JSON encoded as a string, extract the nested `answer` field when possible.\\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, return the best raw text available and say so briefly.\\n\\n5. Return the answer safely.\\n   - Present the nephrology SLM’s answer clearly.\\n   - If useful, add a short plain-language summary.\\n   - Keep uncertainty visible.\\n   - Do not present the SLM output as a confirmed diagnosis.\\n   - If urgent renal or systemic red flags appear, recommend prompt clinician evaluation.\\n\\n## Output pattern\\n\\nReturn:\\n\\n- **Nephrology SLM answer**: the specialist-model answer, lightly cleaned up if needed\\n- **Key takeaway**: short summary in plain language when helpful\\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when clinically relevant or when important data is missing\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_vIxCCH4RCEIWAmSuPpxaAx8K|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8cc00808191a54696653126b165","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\n# Fill this in before using the skill.\nENDPOINT = \"\"\n\n\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return body.strip()\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n    data = parsed.get(\"data\")\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        answer = data.get(\"Answer\") or data.get(\"answer\") or data.get(\"ANSWER\")\n        if answer is not None:\n            if isinstance(answer, str):\n                text = answer.strip()\n                try:\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict) and \"answer\" in nested:\n                        return str(nested[\"answer\"])\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    pass\n                return text\n            return json.dumps(answer, indent=2)\n\n    for key in (\"Answer\", \"answer\", \"ANSWER\"):\n        if key in parsed:\n            value = parsed[key]\n            return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n\ndef call_endpoint(prompt: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\n    if not ENDPOINT.strip():\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            \"SLM nephrology endpoint is not configured. Update ENDPOINT in scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py before using this skill.\"\n        )\n\n    payload = json.dumps({\n        \"metadata\": {\n            \"name\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n            \"workflow_name\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n            \"workflow_type\": \"experiment\",\n            \"workflow_id\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n            \"workflow_run_id\": \"manual\",\n            \"run_id\": \"manual\",\n        },\n        \"data\": {\"prompt\": prompt},\n    }).encode(\"utf-8\")\n\n    req = request.Request(\n        ENDPOINT,\n        data=payload,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            body = resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Request failed: {e}\") from e\n\n    return extract_answer(body)\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Query the nephrology SLM endpoint and print the returned answer\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"prompt\", help=\"Nephrology prompt/brief to send to the model\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=45)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.prompt, timeout=args.timeout)\n    print(answer)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\nfrom urllib import error, request\\n\\n# Fill this in before using the skill.\\nENDPOINT = \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\\n    try:\\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n        return body.strip()\\n\\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n    data = parsed.get(\\\"data\\\")\\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\\n        answer = data.get(\\\"Answer\\\") or data.get(\\\"answer\\\") or data.get(\\\"ANSWER\\\")\\n        if answer is not None:\\n            if isinstance(answer, str):\\n                text = answer.strip()\\n                try:\\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict) and \\\"answer\\\" in nested:\\n                        return str(nested[\\\"answer\\\"])\\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n                    pass\\n                return text\\n            return json.dumps(answer, indent=2)\\n\\n    for key in (\\\"Answer\\\", \\\"answer\\\", \\\"ANSWER\\\"):\\n        if key in parsed:\\n            value = parsed[key]\\n            return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\\n\\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n\\ndef call_endpoint(prompt: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\\n    if not ENDPOINT.strip():\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\n            \\\"SLM nephrology endpoint is not configured. Update ENDPOINT in scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py before using this skill.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    payload = json.dumps({\\n        \\\"metadata\\\": {\\n            \\\"name\\\": \\\"slm-nephrology\\\",\\n            \\\"workflow_name\\\": \\\"slm-nephrology\\\",\\n            \\\"workflow_type\\\": \\\"experiment\\\",\\n            \\\"workflow_id\\\": \\\"slm-nephrology\\\",\\n            \\\"workflow_run_id\\\": \\\"manual\\\",\\n            \\\"run_id\\\": \\\"manual\\\",\\n        },\\n        \\\"data\\\": {\\\"prompt\\\": prompt},\\n    }).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n    req = request.Request(\\n        ENDPOINT,\\n        data=payload,\\n        headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"},\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    try:\\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\\n            body = resp.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\\n        detail = e.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\\\") from e\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Request failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n\\n    return extract_answer(body)\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\\n        description=\\\"Query the nephrology SLM endpoint and print the returned answer\\\"\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"prompt\\\", help=\\\"Nephrology prompt/brief to send to the model\\\")\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--timeout\\\", type=int, default=45)\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n\\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.prompt, timeout=args.timeout)\\n    print(answer)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    try:\\n        main()\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        print(f\\\"ERROR: {exc}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        sys.exit(1)\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_yjk3yfbO6uqBlDuoL2mE7vee|fc_06b4787a018aa87e0169c3e8cc009081918870511f672106f0","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/references/prompt-template.md","content":"# Nephrology brief template\n\nUse this shape when converting the conversation into a compact prompt for the nephrology SLM.\n\n```text\nUser request:\n<the exact question or requested task>\n\nRelevant context:\n- Demographics: <known or unknown>\n- Main problem: <short summary>\n- Symptoms / timeline: <key details>\n- Renal history / PMH: <key details>\n- Medications: <only nephrology-relevant meds>\n- Labs / imaging / urinalysis / pathology: <known findings>\n- Red flags: <if any>\n- Unknowns / missing data: <important gaps>\n\nTask for nephrology SLM:\n<what specific expert help is needed: interpretation, differential, explanation, next-step suggestions, etc.>\n```\n\nGuidance:\n- Keep it compact.\n- Preserve uncertainty.\n- Do not invent values.\n- Include only details that help nephrology reasoning.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/references/prompt-template.md\",\"content\":\"# Nephrology brief template\\n\\nUse this shape when converting the conversation into a compact prompt for the nephrology SLM.\\n\\n```text\\nUser request:\\n<the exact question or requested task>\\n\\nRelevant context:\\n- Demographics: <known or unknown>\\n- Main problem: <short summary>\\n- Symptoms / timeline: <key details>\\n- Renal history / PMH: <key details>\\n- Medications: <only nephrology-relevant meds>\\n- Labs / imaging / urinalysis / pathology: <known findings>\\n- Red flags: <if any>\\n- Unknowns / missing data: <important gaps>\\n\\nTask for nephrology SLM:\\n<what specific expert help is needed: interpretation, differential, explanation, next-step suggestions, etc.>\\n```\\n\\nGuidance:\\n- Keep it compact.\\n- Preserve uncertainty.\\n- Do not invent values.\\n- Include only details that help nephrology reasoning.\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":844,"output":2041,"cacheRead":16000,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18885,"cost":{"input":0.0021100000000000003,"output":0.030615,"cacheRead":0.004,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.036724999999999994}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774446757247}}
